From dfba1287b5f461c8a3f47253a41a2c34d12c6f3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Santos <lsantos7654@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 3 May 2026 16:42:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] Broadcast live-sessions over /presence WS
 (cross-directory fix)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The session pill was driven by Bus.publish(LiveSessionsChanged), but
Bus is per-instance (per-directory). TUIs in different worktrees
subscribe to different instance pubsubs, so a focus update from one
worktree never reached the others. Pill silently desynced across
the multi-worktree workflow.

Make the /presence WebSocket bidirectional. The server's _clients
Map already lives at module scope (correctly cross-directory);
broadcast {type:"live-sessions", sessions} over every connected
WS on each presence change.

The TUI side moves into a small dedicated module (presence-client.ts)
that owns the WS lifecycle, reconnect, and currentFocus tracking.
On every onopen — initial AND reconnect — we re-send currentFocus,
so transient disconnects (and daemon restarts) self-correct without
external nudging. sdk.tsx synthesizes session.live.changed events
from incoming broadcasts so the footer plugin's
api.event.on("session.live.changed", ...) keeps working unchanged.

Adds three server tests (focus broadcast, disconnect broadcast,
cross-directory regression) and a presence-client suite (initial
flush, reconnect re-send, broadcast delivery, close-prevents-
reconnect) — the last two cases exercise daemon restart against a
fresh server on the same port.
